; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Random Composer
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     random, pentatonic, lists, composition, rerandom
; SUMMARY:  Composes a new tune every run with a random walk over a pentatonic scale, arranged in the AABA form of many songs, and draws its shape.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Picking notes completely at random sounds like a cat on a piano.
;   Real melodies mostly move in small steps and come back to ideas
;   they have played before. So this composer takes a random walk,
;   usually one step up or down, sometimes a jump, over the five notes
;   of a pentatonic scale (the black keys of a piano sound like it).
;   It writes phrase A, phrase B, and plays them as A A B A, ending
;   on the home note. The melody is drawn as a line of colored dots.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run several times: every tune is different. Found one you
;   like? Put (rerandom 7) with your favorite number before COMPOSE
;   and you get that same tune every time.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * RANDOM and PICK for chance; RERANDOM to repeat the same "random" tune
;   * a random walk: the next note depends on the one before
;   * keeping a value inside limits so the walk never runs off the scale
;   * musical form: repeating phrases make a tune easy to remember
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Allow bigger jumps by adding 3 and -3 to the moves list.
;   * Use a major scale instead: [262 294 330 349 392 440 494 523 587 659].
;   * Make phrase B start higher than phrase A.
; ============================================================

; Two octaves of the C major pentatonic scale: C D E G A.
make "scale [262 294 330 392 440 523 587 659 784 880]
make "beat 260

; The next position: mostly small steps, now and then a jump.
to next.pos :p
  localmake "q :p + pick [-1 -1 1 1 -2 2 0]
  if :q < 1 [output 2]
  if :q > count :scale [output (count :scale) - 1]
  output :q
end

; A phrase of :n notes, each a list [position beats], starting at :p.
; The last note is long so the phrase sounds finished.
to phrase :n :p
  localmake "out []
  repeat :n - 1 [
    make "out lput (list :p pick [1 1 1 0.5 0.5 2]) :out
    make "p next.pos :p
  ]
  output lput (list :p 2) :out
end

to compose
  make "a phrase 7 6
  make "b phrase 7 8
  ; the final A ends on position 6, the high home C, so it feels complete
  make "end.a lput [6 3] butlast :a
  make "tune (sentence :a :a :b :end.a)
end

; Every note is a dot whose height shows its pitch and whose color
; changes along the scale; a gray line joins the dots.
to perform
  localmake "x -360
  penup setxy :x -200 + 40 * first first :tune pendown
  foreach :tune [
    localmake "spot first ?
    setpencolor 15 setpensize 2
    setxy :x -200 + 40 * :spot
    setpencolor item 1 + remainder :spot 6 [1 2 4 13 14 5]
    setpensize 12 + 6 * last ?
    dot pos
    sound (list item :spot :scale :beat * last ?)
    make "x :x + 25
  ]
end

clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground [250 250 240]
compose
print [Phrase A, as scale positions and beats:]
show :a
print [Phrase B:]
show :b
perform
